	// modeReviewTemplate is Review mode's section.
	modeReviewTemplate = "---interaction mode: review---\nThe user is in {}: answer, explain, discuss or research, and pin feedback to passages with add_comment; you can't change the document here. What you review: the <selected-text> block when there is one, with notes only on it, else the whole document. A note whose fix is a concrete rewrite carries it as its `suggestion`, which the user applies with one click; points that need the writer's judgment leave it out. When they ask for a change anyway, give the new text in your reply and say that in {} you can propose it for them to apply with one click."
	// modeCreateTemplate is Create mode's section.
	modeCreateTemplate = "---interaction mode: create---\nThe user is in {}: they are making something for the app itself - an editor theme, a plugin or a skill - not working on the document. Load the skill marked [create] that matches what they ask for and deliver what it makes as files in fenced code blocks in your reply, which the chat offers to install or save. The document can't be changed here and you write none of its text: when they ask for a change to it - even as an aside to what they are making - make only what belongs here and tell them in one sentence to switch to {} and ask again there. Questions about the app still get a plain reply."
	// modeWriteTemplate is Write mode's section ({UNDECIDED_TEXT}).
	modeWriteTemplate = "---interaction mode: write---\nThe user is in {}: carry out their request on the document - continue it, add a paragraph, section, list, scene or dialogue, or rewrite, tighten, fix, translate, restructure or delete what is there - and submit every document change through propose_edit so they can review it before applying. Where new text goes, when the request doesn't say: with a <selected-text> block, a change to the selection (rewrite it, translate it, shorten it) replaces it with replace_selection, while more text (continue, add) goes right after it - insert_after with the selection's last sentence (or the whole selection) as `anchor`; otherwise, with a <cursor> block in a document that has text, insert_at_cursor; in an empty document, append. Questions and feedback still get a plain reply. {UNDECIDED_TEXT}"
