	findFilesDescriptionWithImages = "Find files in the project folder by name - text files, PDF, Word, PowerPoint, spreadsheet, EPUB and RTF files, and images, marked \"(image)\" (case-insensitive; every word must appear in the path, so \"chapter 3\" finds drafts/chapter-3.md). Markdown and plain-text documents come first. Leave `name` out to list every file, to see what reference material there is - notes, other chapters, pictures; then read_file."
	// readFileDescription is read file description.
	readFileDescription = "Read a text file, or the text of a PDF, Word, PowerPoint, spreadsheet, EPUB or RTF file (as Markdown), from the project folder, by the relative path find_files or search_files shows. A long file comes back in parts: the answer says which lines of how many it shows and where to read on; pass start_line and end_line to read a part - say, a few dozen lines around a line search_files found."
	// readFileDescriptionWithImages is read file description with images.
	readFileDescriptionWithImages = "Read a text file, or the text of a PDF, Word, PowerPoint, spreadsheet, EPUB or RTF file (as Markdown), from the project folder, by the relative path find_files or search_files shows - or look at an image there (PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP, up to 6 MB: a map, a photo, a chart, a scanned page). A long file comes back in parts: the answer says which lines of how many it shows and where to read on; pass start_line and end_line to read a part - say, a few dozen lines around a line search_files found."
